course: dictionary
lesson: 11438
title: Adding one more point
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Additionally is an adverb. It means also, as well, or in addition. Use it to add one more point to what you have already said. «The shop sells apples. Additionally, it sells pears.» The shop sells pears as well as apples.
explain: Additionally can also add an extra amount in maths. «Ella had 5 stickers. Additionally, her friend gave her 2.» Ella had 5, and 2 more were added, so she has 7 now. Additionally tells you to add.
explain: You will see additionally in formal writing and exams, because it sounds clear and organised. Everyday words that mean the same are also, as well and plus. To check, swap one of these into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Additionally means also, as well, or in addition.
fact: It is an adverb, so it often comes at the start of a sentence, followed by a comma.
fact: «Additionally» adds one more point, and it does not change the first point.
fact: Everyday words with a similar meaning: also, as well, plus.
fact: In maths problems, additionally can tell you to add an extra amount to the number you already have.
exercise: «The shop sells apples. Additionally, it sells pears.» What does additionally mean here? | Before | Instead | *Also | Under
exercise: «Ella had 5 stickers. Additionally, her friend gave her 2.» How many stickers does Ella have now? | 3 | *7 | 2 | 10
exercise: Which phrase could replace additionally in formal writing? | Quietly | Because | *In addition | Yesterday
test: «The bus was late. Additionally, it was very cold at the stop.» Which word means the same as additionally here? | Nearly | *As well | Slowly | Sadly
test: Which two words are closest in meaning to additionally? | Yes and no | *Also and as well | Before and after | Under and over
exam: «Tom can swim. Additionally, he can ride a bike.» What does additionally tell you? | It shows the opposite of the first point | *It adds another point | It asks a question | It tells you when something happened
